.TH wsblast-mock 1  "wsblast-mock 0.2.2" 
.SH NAME
wsblast\-mock \- Run a local WebSocket test server: echo with optional delay, jitter, stalls, rejections and closes, or replay of a capture file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwsblast mock\fR [\fB\-\-listen\fR] [\fB\-\-delay\fR] [\fB\-\-jitter\fR] [\fB\-\-close\-after\fR] [\fB\-\-reject\-ratio\fR] [\fB\-\-stall\-every\fR] [\fB\-\-stall\-for\fR] [\fB\-\-replay\fR] [\fB\-\-rules\fR] [\fB\-\-socketio\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a local WebSocket test server: echo with optional delay, jitter, stalls, rejections and closes, or replay of a capture file
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-listen\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR [default: 127.0.0.1:9001]
Address to listen on (host:port; port 0 picks a free port)
.TP
\fB\-\-delay\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 0s]
Hold every reply for this long after its request arrived (e.g. \*(Aq20ms\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-\-jitter\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 0s]
Add a uniformly distributed extra delay between 0 and this to every reply
.TP
\fB\-\-close\-after\fR \fI<N>\fR
Close each connection with code 1000 after it sent N replies
.TP
\fB\-\-reject\-ratio\fR \fI<RATIO>\fR [default: 0]
Answer this fraction (0.0 to 1.0) of upgrade requests with HTTP 503
.TP
\fB\-\-stall\-every\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Stop replying on every connection at each multiple of this period (needs \-\-stall\-for)
.TP
\fB\-\-stall\-for\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
How long each stall lasts; shorter than \-\-stall\-every
.TP
\fB\-\-replay\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Instead of echoing, send each connection the frames a \-\-capture file recorded as received, with their timing
.TP
\fB\-\-rules\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Answer frames as a YAML rules file says: match by text or JSON field, reply from templates, delay or close
.TP
\fB\-\-socketio\fR
Speak Socket.IO (Engine.IO 4): accept any namespace, acknowledge every event that asks for an ack with its arguments, echo the others, and ping every 25s
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-cert\fR \fI<PEM>\fR
PEM certificate chain to serve wss:// instead of ws:// (clients must trust it, e.g. with SSL_CERT_FILE)
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-key\fR \fI<PEM>\fR
PEM private key for \-\-tls\-cert
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.2
